## Advisory notes (non-blocking, for follow-up)

1. VISUAL FOCUS INDICATOR MISSING: data-focused attribute is set on the active row
   but no CSS styles it. DIRECTION.md SS5 prescribes "2px verdigris at 2px offset"
   focus ring. The keyboard logic works (tested) but the user receives no visual
   feedback of which item is focused. Recommend adding a [data-focused="true"]
   CSS rule in a follow-up opus.

2. OPERA NOT RENDERED: InboxView accepts opera in props and checks opera.length
   for the empty state, but does not render opera rows. Brief says "Opera are
   display-only: listed in the queue but not actionable." No behaviour tests opera
   rendering, so this is not a behaviour failure, but the brief's prose implies
   they should appear. This is acceptable for Web I since opera rendering details
   are unspecified.

3. SELLA ID LINE-HEIGHT: The data type role (mono 12/18) should have explicit
   lineHeight: "18px". Currently inherits from the row's 40px height context.
   Functionally fine; typographically imprecise.

4. AGE NUMERAL: DIRECTION.md SS6 describes "age as a right-aligned mono numeral
   that escalates in weight (500 -> 700) with age." Not implemented; brief
   behaviour 4 does not require it. Acceptable omission for Web I.

5. COLOPHON COMMENT: Colophon.tsx header references "DIRECTION.md SS4.4" but the
   colophon is SS4.5. Trivial comment error.
